---
import Illustration from "../ui/Illustration.astro";
import Button from "../ui/Button.astro";
import { routes } from "../../data/navigation";
---

<div class="problem container" id="the-problem">
  <div class="section-title problem__head">
    <h2 class="problem__label" data-lines>The problem</h2>
    <span class="section-title__rule"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="problem__body">
    <Illustration name="child" class="problem__illus" label="A child writing at a desk" speed={2} />
    <div class="problem__text">
      <h3 class="problem__title" data-lines>Learning outcomes are decided long before a child sits an exam</h3>
      <div class="problem__paras">
        <p>We know where learners end up, but we know far less about what shapes their journey there.</p>
        <p>
          Attainment data can show us learning outcomes, but it does not tell us whether a child has the support they
          need at home, whether they are safe and consistently present in school, whether good teachers have the
          conditions to remain in the profession, or whether a student can afford to continue their education.
        </p>
        <p>These factors have a profound influence on learning, yet they remain largely unmeasured.</p>
        <p>
          Without this context, programmes risk being built on assumptions about the problems learners face rather than
          evidence about what is actually shaping their experiences and outcomes.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Button href={routes.theProblem} label="Read the full picture" class="problem__cta--long" />
      <Button href={routes.theProblem} label="Read full picture" class="problem__cta--short" />
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .problem {
    max-width: calc(1127.5px + var(--gutter) * 2);
    padding-top: 96px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 66px;
  }
  .problem__label {
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .problem__body {
    display: flex;
    gap: 32px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .problem__body :global(.problem__illus) {
    width: 298px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .problem__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 690px;
  }
  .problem__title {
    max-width: 499px;
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }
  .problem__paras {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 28px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .problem__paras p:nth-child(3) {
    margin-top: -8px;
  }
  /* Phone wording of the button */
  .problem__text :global(.problem__cta--short) {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Tablets: Figma 768 frame (illustration beside the text, smaller type) */
  @media (min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px) {
    .problem {
      padding-top: 64px;
      padding-bottom: 64px;
      gap: 40px;
    }
    .problem__body :global(.problem__illus) {
      width: 275px;
    }
    .problem__text {
      gap: 20px;
    }
    .problem__title {
      font-size: 24px;
      letter-spacing: 0.288px;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .problem__paras {
      gap: 20px;
    }
  }
  /* Phones: Figma 390 frame */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .problem {
      gap: 28px;
      padding-top: 48px;
      padding-bottom: 48px;
    }
    .problem__label {
      font-size: 20px;
      letter-spacing: 0.24px;
    }
    .problem__body {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 28px;
    }
    .problem__body :global(.problem__illus) {
      width: 275px;
      align-self: center;
    }
    .problem__title {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: 20px;
      letter-spacing: 0.24px;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .problem__paras {
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 18px;
      gap: 18px;
      color: var(--ink);
      opacity: 0.8;
    }
    .problem__text {
      gap: 16px;
    }
    .problem__text :global(.problem__cta--long) {
      display: none;
    }
    .problem__text :global(.problem__cta--short) {
      display: inline-flex;
    }
  }
</style>
